---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Witchly: Scaling a free game-server platform to 10,000 users | Tushar A."
  description="How Tushar built Witchly.host: 10,000+ users on bare-metal Hetzner, €100/mo, mitigated 50 Gbps L7 DDoS in <20 minutes via three-tier plane separation."
  pageType="article"
  keywords="Witchly, game server hosting, free hosting, Hetzner bare-metal, Docker, Pterodactyl, DDoS mitigation, three-tier architecture, Tushar A."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="container case">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to home</a>

    <article class="sketch case-head reveal">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">/case-study</p>
      <h1 class="case-title">Witchly</h1>
      <p class="case-deck">
        A free game-server hosting platform on bare-metal Hetzner. 10,000+ users,
        bootstrapped, €100/mo infra. Plus the time a 50 Gbps L7 DDoS hit and we
        recovered in under 20 minutes with zero data loss.
      </p>
      <div class="case-meta">
        <span>August 2021 - Present</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <span>Founder & Lead Systems Engineer</span>
        <span class="dot">·</span>
        <a href="https://witchly.host" target="_blank" rel="noopener">witchly.host →</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="case-stats reveal" aria-label="Witchly stats">
      <div class="case-stats-row">
        <div class="case-stat">
          <span class="case-stat-value">10,000+</span>
          <span class="case-stat-label">Registered users</span>
        </div>
        <div class="case-stat">
          <span class="case-stat-value good">50 Gbps+</span>
          <span class="case-stat-label">DDoS mitigated</span>
        </div>
        <div class="case-stat">
          <span class="case-stat-value">€100/mo</span>
          <span class="case-stat-label">Infra cost</span>
        </div>
        <div class="case-stat">
          <span class="case-stat-value">$3K+/mo</span>
          <span class="case-stat-label">Equiv. AWS cost</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="sketch case-intro reveal">
      <p>
        Game-server hosting sits in an awkward gap. Free platforms like Aternos and
        Minehut are severely resource-constrained and unreliable under load. Commercial
        hosts charge $15–30 per server per month, pricing out hobbyists and small
        communities entirely. Nobody was offering production-grade, low-latency
        infrastructure at zero cost.
      </p>
      <p>
        Witchly was built to close that gap, and to do it on zero external funding.
        Every architectural decision maximises raw compute per euro so the free tier
        is economically viable long-term. The full case study below walks through the
        stack, the DDoS incident, and the cost economics.
        <strong>The PDF renders inline; you can also <a href="/Case-Study/Witchly-scaling.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">download it directly</a>.</strong>
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="sketch case-pdf reveal" aria-label="Witchly case study PDF">
      <object
        data="/Case-Study/Witchly-scaling.pdf"
        type="application/pdf"
        class="pdf-frame"
        aria-label="Witchly case study"
      >
        <div class="pdf-fallback">
          <p>
            Your browser can't display the PDF inline.
            <a href="/Case-Study/Witchly-scaling.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Download the case study →
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </object>
    </article>

    <section class="case-stack-wrap reveal">
      <h2 class="section-h">Stack at a glance</h2>
      <div class="stack-grid">
        <div class="note note-mint stack-item" style="--tilt:-1.2deg">
          <p class="stack-h">Hardware</p>
          <p class="stack-b">Hetzner bare-metal: Intel i9-9900K, 128 GB RAM, 2 TB NVMe. Ubuntu 20.04, in Germany and Finland.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note note-pink stack-item" style="--tilt:1deg">
          <p class="stack-h">Orchestration</p>
          <p class="stack-b">Docker + Pterodactyl. Tenant isolation enforced at the kernel via cgroup CPU pinning and hard RAM limits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note note-violet stack-item" style="--tilt:-0.6deg">
          <p class="stack-h">Architecture</p>
          <p class="stack-b">Three independently-scalable planes: frontend, control plane, data plane. Game UDP/TCP bypasses the control plane entirely.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note note-yellow stack-item" style="--tilt:1.4deg">
          <p class="stack-h">Custom dashboard</p>
          <p class="stack-b">Built from scratch: server provisioning, native Stripe billing, real-time per-server CPU/RAM/storage, internal REST APIs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note note-mint stack-item" style="--tilt:-1deg">
          <p class="stack-h">DDoS defence</p>
          <p class="stack-b">Layered: Cloudflare WAF at the edge, AS-level filtering at the CDN, host-level UFW + Fail2Ban with default-deny.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note note-pink stack-item" style="--tilt:0.8deg">
          <p class="stack-h">Cost</p>
          <p class="stack-b">€100/mo for the full cluster vs $3,000+/mo for equivalent EC2 + Shield Advanced. The delta makes the free tier viable.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="note note-yellow case-cta reveal" style="--tilt:-0.8deg">
      <h2>Want to chat about scaling, hosting, or DDoS engineering?</h2>
      <div class="case-cta-row">
        <a href="/#contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="/Case-Study/Witchly-scaling.pdf" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Download PDF
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .case {
    padding-top: 110px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
    max-width: 1060px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .back-link:hover { color: var(--violet-ink); }

  .case-head,
  .case-intro,
  .case-pdf { margin-bottom: 32px; }

  .case-head { padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); }

  .case-title {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 4px 0 14px;
  }

  .case-deck {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.12rem);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .case-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .case-meta a {
    color: var(--violet-ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: underline wavy color-mix(in srgb, var(--violet-ink) 40%, transparent);
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .case-stats { margin-bottom: 40px; }

  .case-stats-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .case-stat-value {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .case-stat-value.good { color: var(--good); }

  .case-stat-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .case-stats-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }

  .case-intro p { color: var(--muted); }
  .case-intro p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .case-intro strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .case-intro a { color: var(--violet-ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .case-pdf { padding: 10px; }

  .pdf-frame {
    width: 100%;
    height: 85vh;
    min-height: 600px;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #fff;
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .pdf-frame { height: 70vh; min-height: 420px; }
  }

  .pdf-fallback {
    padding: 60px 30px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .pdf-fallback a { color: var(--violet-ink); font-weight: 700; }

  .case-stack-wrap { margin-top: 64px; }

  .section-h {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .stack-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 290px), 1fr));
    gap: 40px 28px;
  }

  .stack-h {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .stack-b { font-size: 0.95rem; color: #3d3829; }

  .case-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(36px, 5vw, 52px);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 72px auto 0;
  }

  .case-cta h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .case-cta-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 14px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
</style>
